Mezery
******

.[perex]
Sekce `spacing` rozhoduje o mezerách na řádku: kolem operátorů, za čárkou, uvnitř závorek, mezi jménem funkce a závorkou, za klíčovým slovem, kolem `->` a `::`, v deklaraci typu a v komentáři.

U mezer je hodnotou tvar a každý tvar má slovo i ukázku kódu. Do konfigurace můžete napsat kterékoli z nich, a ukázka se čte nejlíp, protože říká přesně to, co uvidíte v kódu:

```neon
spacing:
	concatenation: '$a.$b'
	arrowFunction: 'fn ($x) => $x'
	cast: '(int) $x'
	catchTypes: 'catch (A|B $e)'
```

Ukázku DressCode nečte jako kód, jen ji porovná s ukázkami, které klíč zná; zapsat ji lze i slovem, `concatenation: compact`. Neznámá ukázka je chyba, která vypíše ty známé.

```php .[before]
$label = 'Item '.$name . ' x'.$count;  // Expected no whitespace before the `.` operator. // Expected no whitespace after the `.` operator.
$double = fn($x) => $x * 2;  // Expected a single space after the `fn` keyword.
$id = (int)$row['id'];  // Expected a single space after the cast.
```

```php .[after]
$label = 'Item '.$name.' x'.$count;
$double = fn ($x) => $x * 2;
$id = (int) $row['id'];
```

Mezera kolem operátoru, který stojí na zlomu řádku, je věc odsazení a sekce [multiline |multiline], ne téhle. Kde víc mezer zarovnává sloupce, rozhodují parametry `binaryOperatorAlignment`, `commaAlignment` a `ternaryAlignment`, jestli zarovnání smí zůstat; DressCode sloupce sám nikdy nezarovnává.


spacing.arrayBrackets
=====================

The whitespace inside the brackets of an array.

- `compact` nebo `'[1, 2]'`: none inside
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `trim_array_spaces`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Arrays.SingleLineArrayWhitespace` .[decision-facts]


spacing.classHead
=================

The spaces between the words of the head of a class declaration, which stays on one line unless a comment breaks it, the brace and the implemented interfaces being free to take the next one.

- `spaced` nebo `'class Foo extends Bar implements Baz'`: single spaces
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spaced`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `spaced`, symfony `spaced` · pokrývá `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration`, `PSR2.Classes.ClassDeclaration.SpaceBeforeKeyword` .[decision-facts]


spacing.anonymousClass
======================

The space between `class` and the arguments of an anonymous class.

- `spaced` nebo `'new class ($a)'`: a single space before the arguments
- `compact` nebo `'new class($a)'`: no space before the arguments
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spaced`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `spaced`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `class_definition`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration`, `PSR2.Classes.ClassDeclaration.SpaceBeforeKeyword` .[decision-facts]


spacing.comment
===============

The space after the marker of a comment and before the closing one, unless another `/` or `*` follows the marker, as in a `////` ruler; doc comments are the matter of the phpDoc rules.

- `spaced` nebo `'// text'`: a single space after the marker
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `spaced`, symfony `spaced` · pokrývá `PhpCsFixerCustomFixers/comment_surrounded_by_spaces`, `single_line_comment_spacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.commentAfterCode
========================

The whitespace before a comment that follows code on its line.

- `spaced` nebo `'$a; // text'`: at least one space
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `spaced`, symfony `spaced` · pokrývá `PhpCsFixerCustomFixers/comment_surrounded_by_spaces`, `single_line_comment_spacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.commentAfterCodeAlignment
=================================

Whether a comment following code may be aligned by more spaces.

- `any`: more spaces stay
- `none`: exactly one space

Parametr, výchozí `any` · standardy: perCs `any`, psr12 `any`, nette `any`, symfony `any` · pokrývá `PhpCsFixerCustomFixers/comment_surrounded_by_spaces`, `single_line_comment_spacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.switchCase
==================

The whitespace before the colon of a `case`.

- `compact` nebo `'case 1:'`: none before the colon
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `compact`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `switch_case_space`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.SwitchDeclaration`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.SwitchDeclaration.SpaceBeforeColonCASE` .[decision-facts]


spacing.binaryOperator
======================

The spaces around a binary operator other than `.`, an assignment, `instanceof`, `=>` and the `=` of a default, unless it sits at a line break; an assignment and `=>` stay on the line of what is before them, `instanceof` and what follows a comparison, a bitwise operator or a shift on the line of the operator, unless the line would grow too wide.

- `spaced` nebo `'$a + $b'`: a single space around
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spaced`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `spaced`, symfony `spaced` · pokrývá `binary_operator_spaces`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.LogicalOperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.OperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]

Týká se aritmetických, porovnávacích, logických a bitových operátorů, `??`, přiřazení včetně `+=` a `??=`, `instanceof`, `=>` a `=` výchozí hodnoty. Tečka má vlastní klíč `concatenation`, protože o ní se styly rozcházejí.

```neon
spacing:
	binaryOperator: '$a + $b'
```

```php .[before]
$total=$price*$count;  // Expected at least one space before the `=` operator. // Expected at least one space after the `=` operator. // Expected at least one space before the `*` operator. // Expected at least one space after the `*` operator.
$label = $count>1 ? 'items' : 'item';  // Expected at least one space before the `>` operator. // Expected at least one space after the `>` operator.
$map = ['a'=>1, 'b' => 2];  // Expected at least one space before the double arrow. // Expected at least one space after the double arrow.
$aligned   = 1;
$alsoFine  = 2;
```

```php .[after]
$total = $price * $count;
$label = $count > 1 ? 'items' : 'item';
$map = ['a' => 1, 'b' => 2];
$aligned   = 1;
$alsoFine  = 2;
```

Poslední dva řádky zůstaly: zarovnání mezerami dovoluje výchozí hodnota parametru `binaryOperatorAlignment`.


spacing.binaryOperatorAlignment
===============================

Which whitespace wider than a single space around an operator stays, aligning a column of assignments or of array items; alignment is never made.

- `none`: more spaces collapse to one
- `spaces`: spaces aligning a column stay
- `tabs`: tabs aligning a column stay
- `any`: any alignment stays

Parametr, výchozí `spaces` · standardy: perCs `spaces`, psr12 `spaces`, nette `spaces`, symfony `none` · pokrývá `binary_operator_spaces`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.LogicalOperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.OperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]

```neon
spacing:
	binaryOperator: '$a + $b'
	binaryOperatorAlignment: none
```

```php .[before]
$aligned   = 1;  // Expected a single space before the `=` operator.
$alsoFine  = 2;  // Expected a single space before the `=` operator.
```

```php .[after]
$aligned = 1;
$alsoFine = 2;
```


spacing.cast
============

The space between a cast and its operand, which stays on the line of the cast.

- `spaced` nebo `'(int) $x'`: a single space after the cast
- `compact` nebo `'(int)$x'`: no space after the cast
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spaced`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `spaced`, symfony `spaced` · pokrývá `cast_spaces` .[decision-facts]


spacing.concatenation
=====================

The space around the concatenation operator, unless it sits at a line break.

- `spaced` nebo `'$a . $b'`: a single space around
- `compact` nebo `'$a.$b'`: no space around
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spaced`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `spaced`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `concat_space`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.Strings.ConcatenationSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.doubleColon
===================

The whitespace around the double colon.

- `compact` nebo `'Foo::bar()'`: none around
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `compact`, symfony `keep` · pokrývá `no_space_around_double_colon`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.ScopeKeywordSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.objectOperator
======================

The whitespace around the object operator.

- `compact` nebo `'$a->b()'`: none around
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `object_operator_without_whitespace`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.ObjectOperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.offsetBrackets
======================

The whitespace around and inside the brackets of an offset access.

- `compact` nebo `'$a[0]'`: none around and inside
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `no_spaces_around_offset`, `Squiz.Arrays.ArrayBracketSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.reference
=================

The whitespace between `&` and its operand.

- `compact` nebo `'&$x'`: none between
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `compact`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `SlevomatCodingStandard.Operators.ReferenceSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.spread
==============

The whitespace between `...` and its operand.

- `compact` nebo `'...$x'`: none between
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `compact`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `SlevomatCodingStandard.Operators.SpreadOperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.ternary
===============

The whitespace around `?` and `:` of a ternary, and around `?:` as a whole, unless the operator sits at a line break.

- `spaced` nebo `'$a ? $b : $c'`: whitespace around `?` and `:`
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spaced`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `spaced`, symfony `spaced` · pokrývá `ternary_operator_spaces`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.ternaryAlignment
========================

Whether more spaces around `?` and `:` stay.

- `any`: more spaces stay
- `none`: exactly one space

Parametr, výchozí `any` · standardy: perCs `any`, psr12 `any`, nette `none`, symfony `any` · pokrývá `ternary_operator_spaces`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.unaryOperator
=====================

The whitespace between a unary operator and its operand, which stay on one line, and inside a variable variable, `$$a` and `${'a'}`.

- `compact` nebo `'-$x'`: no space after the operator
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `compact`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `unary_operator_spaces`, `Generic.WhiteSpace.IncrementDecrementSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Operators.NegationOperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.OperatorSpacing.Unary` .[decision-facts]


spacing.unaryOperatorsWithSpace
===============================

The operators whose operand may stand apart from them, as written, `! $x`.

- seznam z těchto slov:
	- `++`: increment
	- `--`: decrement
	- `!`: negation
	- `-`: minus
	- `+`: plus
	- `~`: bitwise negation
	- `@`: error suppression

Parametr, výchozí `[]` · standardy: perCs `['!']`, psr12 `['!']`, nette `[]`, symfony `[]` · pokrývá `Generic.WhiteSpace.IncrementDecrementSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Operators.NegationOperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.OperatorSpacing.Unary` .[decision-facts]


spacing.declare
===============

The whitespace inside a `declare` statement.

- `compact` nebo `'declare(strict_types=1)'`: none inside
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `compact`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `declare_equal_normalize`, `declare_parentheses`, `PSR12.Files.DeclareStatement` .[decision-facts]


spacing.call
============

The whitespace between the name of a function and its parenthesis, of a call and of a declaration alike.

- `compact` nebo `'foo($a, $b)'`: no space before the parenthesis
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `compact`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `no_spaces_after_function_name`, `Generic.Functions.FunctionCallArgumentSpacing.SpaceBeforeOpenBracket`, `PSR2.Methods.FunctionCallSignature`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.namedArgument
=====================

The whitespace around the colon of a named argument.

- `spacedAfter` nebo `'foo(name: $x)'`: none before the colon, a single space after
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spacedAfter`, psr12 `keep`, nette `spacedAfter`, symfony `spacedAfter` · pokrývá `SlevomatCodingStandard.Functions.NamedArgumentSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.typeDeclaration
=======================

The whitespace of a type declaration, which stays on one line with what it describes: none inside a type, a single space between a type and the name it declares, `): int` for a return type and `enum Suit: string` for a backing type.

- `compact` nebo `'?int $x'`: none inside a type, a single space before the name
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `compact`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `compact_nullable_type_declaration`, `return_type_declaration`, `PSR12.Functions.NullableTypeDeclaration`, `PSR12.Functions.ReturnTypeDeclaration`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Classes.BackedEnumTypeSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ParameterTypeHintSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.PropertyTypeHintSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ReturnTypeHintSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.catchTypes
==================

The space around the bar between the types of a `catch`.

- `spaced` nebo `'catch (A | B $e)'`: a single space around the bar
- `compact` nebo `'catch (A|B $e)'`: no space around the bar
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `compact_nullable_type_declaration`, `return_type_declaration`, `PSR12.Functions.NullableTypeDeclaration`, `PSR12.Functions.ReturnTypeDeclaration`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Classes.BackedEnumTypeSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ParameterTypeHintSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.PropertyTypeHintSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ReturnTypeHintSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.attribute
=================

The whitespace inside the brackets of an attribute group and before the parenthesis of its arguments.

- `compact` nebo `'#[Foo($a)]'`: none inside the brackets, none before the parenthesis
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `compact`, psr12 `keep`, nette `compact`, symfony `compact` · pokrývá `attribute_block_no_spaces` .[decision-facts]


spacing.comma
=============

The whitespace around a comma, which stays on the line of what is before it, a line ending after it being free.

- `spacedAfter` nebo `'$a, $b'`: none before, a single space after
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spacedAfter`, psr12 `spacedAfter`, nette `spacedAfter`, symfony `spacedAfter` · pokrývá `no_whitespace_before_comma_in_array`, `whitespace_after_comma_in_array`, `Generic.Functions.FunctionCallArgumentSpacing`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclarationArgumentSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.commaAlignment
======================

Which whitespace wider than a single space after a comma stays, aligning the columns of a table; alignment is never made.

- `tabs`: tabs aligning a column stay
- `spaces`: spaces aligning a column stay
- `any`: any alignment stays
- `none`: more whitespace collapses to a single space

Parametr, výchozí `tabs` · standardy: perCs `none`, psr12 `none`, nette `tabs`, symfony `any` · pokrývá `no_whitespace_before_comma_in_array`, `whitespace_after_comma_in_array`, `Generic.Functions.FunctionCallArgumentSpacing`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclarationArgumentSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.languageConstruct
=========================

The space after `return`, `throw`, `yield`, `print`, `include`, `clone`, `new` and the other keywords followed by code, which also stays on their line, and inside the braces of abbreviated property hooks; the braces of a group use hug their names.

- `spaced` nebo `'return $x'`: a single space
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spaced`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `spaced`, symfony `spaced` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `single_space_around_construct`, `Generic.WhiteSpace.LanguageConstructSpacing`, `PSR12.Traits.UseDeclaration`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.SwitchDeclaration`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Functions.ArrowFunctionDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.controlKeyword
======================

The space after `if`, `elseif`, `while`, `for`, `foreach`, `switch`, `match` and `catch`, and before the brace or the body a structure opens on its line; the colon of the alternative syntax hugs what is before it.

- `spaced` nebo `'if ($a)'`: a single space
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Požadavek · standardy: perCs `spaced`, psr12 `spaced`, nette `spaced`, symfony `spaced` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `single_space_around_construct`, `Generic.WhiteSpace.LanguageConstructSpacing`, `PSR12.Traits.UseDeclaration`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.SwitchDeclaration`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Functions.ArrowFunctionDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.connectingKeyword
